---@class posthog.metrics.MetricSamplesBody
---@field metricName? string Exact metric name to list raw emissions for (e.g. 'http.server.duration'). Omit to list emissions across all metric names — allowed only with traceId (the trace->metrics pivot).
---@field dateFrom string Lower bound (inclusive) for the sample window. ISO 8601.
---@field dateTo? string Upper bound (exclusive) for the sample window. Defaults to now if omitted.
---@field traceId? string Restrict to emissions on this trace (hex trace id, as the tracing product uses) — the reverse metric->trace pivot. Omit for all traces.
---@field spanId? string Restrict to emissions recorded on this span (hex span id). Requires traceId, since a span id is only unique within its trace.
---@field metricType? posthog.metrics.OtelMetricTypeEnum|string|distilled.Null Constrain the emissions to one metric type. A name can exist as several types (e.g. a counter and a gauge); without this, emissions of every type sharing the name are listed together. Pass the same value used for the chart so both describe the same series. * `gauge` - gauge * `sum` - sum * `histogram` - histogram * `exponential_histogram` - exponential_histogram * `summary` - summary
---@field filters? posthog.metrics.MetricSamplesBodyFiltersList Label predicates ANDed together, matched against each emission's series. Pass the same filters used for the chart so the emissions listed are the ones behind it.
---@field limit? number Max emissions to return, newest first. Defaults to 100, capped at 1000.

